# A gitignore `#` only starts a comment at the START of a line — an inline `#` after a
# pattern becomes part of the pattern. These were silently broken as trailing-comment
# lines, so the guards below never matched. Keep comments on their own lines.

# matcher shortlists.json / picks.json — contains subscriber PII
exchange/
# Cloudflare Origin Certificate + private key (see deploy/cert-renewal.md)
deploy/origin/
# never commit a certificate or private key
*.pem

# Playwright MCP scratch output (page snapshots, console logs) from local UI walk-throughs
.playwright-mcp/

# Local-only infrastructure reference (VPS IP, Cloudflare zone/account IDs).
# Public notes refer to these by placeholder; see notes/INFRA.local.md.
notes/INFRA.local.md

# `scripts/matchspans.py --dump` corpus cache: ~60k (category, title) rows pulled from
# production. Public job titles only — the query touches `postings`, never `profiles` — but a
# corpus extract is a measurement, not a repo artefact, and it is stale the next morning.
scripts/.corpus-titles.csv

# ATS-discovery output CSVs (`discover_ats.py`, `discover_seed.py`). Each is a point-in-time
# probe of live boards, not a repo artefact — stale within a day — and a default run writing one
# into the tree is how a discovery run silently made `deploy.sh` refuse a "dirty tree".
scripts/seed_candidates.csv
scripts/ats_discovery_results.csv
scripts/*_ats_discovery.csv
scripts/*_discovery.csv

# The whole notes/ tree is local-only as of 2026-09-23.
#
# It was removed from this repo's history when the repo was made public: the session logs
# carried real subscriber addresses, one note identifying two subscribers by their
# relationship, and the production VPS IP — security rule 1, committed 181 times over.
# They remain on disk (and in the pre-publication mirror) because CLAUDE.md cites them as
# reasoning, but a public repo is the one place they must never go. Ignore the directory
# rather than individual files: a per-file list is a copy, and the next note nobody adds to
# the copy is the one that leaks.
notes/

# The personal weekly feed (2026-09-23). A second JobDigest instance for the owner's own
# inbox, reading sources this product excludes on terms — Alma Career (jobs.cz, profesia),
# SmartRecruiters and StartupJobs. It runs against its own database (`jobmatch_personal`)
# that the api/web containers cannot see, and it never touches `gather()`, so
# `ingestion/tests/test_source_exclusions.py` is unchanged and still binding.
#
# Ignored because this repo is PUBLIC. A risk decision the owner made about their own
# exposure is not a thing to publish as code, and `deploy.sh` ships via `git archive` — so
# ignoring it is also what stops it ever riding a deploy into the product image. It is
# rsynced to /opt/jobdigest-personal and mounted at run time instead. See personal/README.md.
personal/
